### ============================================
### WEBSERV: FILE DELETE HANDLER TEST SUITE
### ============================================
### Description: Tests for handling DELETE requests to remove files.
### Assumes a server on port 8080 with a location like:
###   location /delete/ {
###       allow_methods DELETE;
###       root /var/www/delete_zone;
###   }
### Also assumes a directory structure on the server:
###   /var/www/delete_zone/
###     - deletable_file.txt
###     - protected_file.txt (chmod 444, in a writable directory)
###     /a_directory/
###     /no_parent_write_perms/ (chmod 555)
###       - unreachable.txt
### ============================================

### Variables
@host = localhost
@port = 8080
@baseUrl = http://{{host}}:{{port}}
@userAgent = WebServ-Test-Client/1.0

### ============================================
### Section 1: Successful Deletion
### ============================================

### Test 1.1: Delete an existing, accessible file
# PRE-REQUISITE: Create a file at /var/www/delete_zone/deletable_file.txt
# EXPECTS: 204 No Content. The response body should be empty.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/delete/deletable_file.txt
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### ============================================
### Section 2: Client Error Handling (4xx)
### ============================================

### Test 2.1: File Not Found
# Attempting to delete a file that does not exist.
# EXPECTS: 404 Not Found
DELETE